# .cursorrules
# Best Bike Paths (BBP) — Project rules, repo policy, and AI integration rules
# Version: 2.0

########################################
# PURPOSE
########################################
# This file lists rules, expectations, repository conventions, and AI project assistant rules for the Best Bike Paths (BBP) R&DD project.
# It applies to all team members, deliverables (RASD, DD), code, models (UML/Alloy), docs, and any automated artifacts.
# Everyone in the group must follow these rules.

########################################
# SCOPE
########################################
# Applies to all project activities: mobile app integration, backend services, end-to-end testing documentation, sequence diagrams, CI/CD, and all repository artifacts.

########################################
# ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES
########################################
- Team lead: coordinates deadlines, repo organization, final submissions.
- Commit owners: responsible for their commits and meaningful commit messages.
- Reviewer: at least one member reviews major commits/PRs before merging to `main`.
- Pablo: responsible for mobile client integration, end-to-end flows, service-to-service integration, test case design, and sequence diagrams.

########################################
# COMMUNICATION
########################################
- Primary channel: project GitHub issues and repository discussions.
- Urgent matters: direct message (WhatsApp/Telegram/email) and open an issue with summary.
- Post general questions on the course forum (WeBeep) for visibility.

########################################
# REPOSITORY ORGANIZATION
########################################
- Root must contain: `README.md`, `DeliveryFolder/`, `RASD/`, `DD/`, `models/`.
- `DeliveryFolder` contains final PDFs: `RASDv1.pdf`, `DDv1.pdf`, etc.
- Use `main` as protected branch. Development on feature branches: `feature/<short-description>` or `task/<id>-<short>`.
- No direct pushes to `main` except by the final submitter.

########################################
# COMMIT & PR RULES
########################################
- Commit messages: `TYPE(scope): short description` (e.g., `feat(rasd): add use case for trip recording`).
- Small, atomic commits attributable to the author.
- PRs required for any change affecting deliverables or shared models, with at least one approving review.

########################################
# DELIVERABLES & DEADLINES
########################################
- Respect course deadlines: registration, RASD, DD.
- Push final PDFs to `DeliveryFolder` before 23:59 Rome time on the deadline date.
- For updates, push `RASDv2.pdf` or `DDv2.pdf` with a "Changes" section.

########################################
# CODE STYLE & QUALITY
########################################
- Keep code/readme comments in English.
- Consistent formatting; document style in `README.md`.
- Include minimal tests or example runs for scripts/tools.

########################################
# NAMING CONVENTIONS & LANGUAGE
########################################
- All folder, file, document, and artifact names MUST be in English.
- Examples: `ch##_descriptive_name.tex`, `DD.tex`.
- Applies to all deliverables, code, models, documentation, scripts.

########################################
# TESTING & CI
########################################
- Optional but recommended: simple CI (GitHub Actions) to validate builds, UML/Alloy artifacts, or PDF presence before merge.

########################################
# TIME TRACKING & EFFORT REPORT
########################################
- Track hours per member for each deliverable. Include effort table in RASD and DD ("Effort Spent").
- Save logs in `docs/time_logs/` as CSV or markdown.

########################################
# LATE SUBMISSION & PENALTIES
########################################
- Notify professor if delay is expected.
- Small delays tolerated with prior notice; otherwise penalty applies.

########################################
# ACADEMIC INTEGRITY
########################################
- All work must be original or correctly cited. Plagiarism or falsified logs reported and may result in failing the project.

########################################
# BACKUPS & PRIVACY
########################################
- Keep local copies of final PDFs and models. Use fallback repo if GitHub privacy issues arise, report URL to professor.

########################################
# AI INTEGRATION RULES (CURSOR CONTEXT)
########################################
- Language: All outputs must be in English.
- Maintain project context at all times:
  - Project: Best Bike Paths (BBP)
  - Purpose: Mobile app for cyclists, route search, trip logging, automatic ride detection, obstacle detection, reviews, statistics.
  - Architecture: Mobile iOS/Android client (GPS, accelerometer, gyroscope), backend microservices, PostgreSQL + Redis, API Gateway, RabbitMQ, external APIs (weather, maps, email)
  - Backend services: User Management, Trip Management, Path Management, Sensor Processing, Path Search, Rating, Information Merging
  - Pablo’s responsibility: Mobile integration, end-to-end flows, test cases, sequence diagrams
- Reference context before generating outputs.
- Clarify ambiguous requirements before producing content.
- Suggest best practices for integration, testing, and error handling.
- Bottom-up approach: start from components, then E2E flows.
- Output formatting: structured markdown, tables, bullet points, Mermaid for diagrams.
- Label outputs clearly: [UCx], [Mobile-Server], [Service-to-Service], [Test Cases].
- Retain memory of previous UC, test cases, diagrams for continuity.
- Coordinate with José for backend context when needed.

########################################
# CHANGES
########################################
- Any changes must be agreed by all team members and recorded with date and reason.

END